WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 9: City Places.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.040
In this unit, your child learns the words for places in
a town — the shop, the market, the school, the hospital,

3
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:12.720
the mosque.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:20.360
They learn the people who work in these places, and simple
words that tell us where things are (near, far, next to).

5
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.640
They also meet the traffic lights and learn
that red means stop and green means go.

6
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.800
The big idea is that a town is full
of helpful places and kind people,

7
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.020
and that we all help keep our town clean and safe.

8
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.960
The goal is warm, confident English — not perfect spelling.

9
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.940
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:52.180
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name places
in a town (shop, market, school, hospital, mosque, park).

11
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.060
you will also name some people who
help us (teacher, doctor, shopkeeper).

12
00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:02.580
you will also say where a place is using
position words (near, next to, here, there).

13
00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.020
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:12.120
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
shop, market, school, hospital, mosque, park.

15
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.300
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:21.120
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:26.800
The reading sequence includes A Walk
Around Town and Talk about City Places.

18
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.640
Read actively.

19
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.760
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.840
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:43.280
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

22
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:49.500
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: There is a ___.

23
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:57.720
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.700
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:08.420
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.080
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.880
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.760
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:24.220
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.980
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:32.900
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
